  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The demolition of the dwelling, save for the front fa�ade, would result in less than substantial harm to the significance of the Locally Listed Building and the West Wimbledon Conservation Area. There are not considered to be public benefits that outweigh this harm. As such the proposal is in conflict with Merton Local Plan Policy D12.5, London Plan policy HC1, NPPF para 216 (re non-designated heritage assets), and NPPF para 212 (in respect of designated heritage assets).",
    "Reason : 2 - In the absence of a legal agreement to secure the self-build or custom-build exemption in relation to Biodiversity Net Gain (BNG), the proposed development fails to demonstrate compliance with the requirements of the Environment Act 2021. Without such an agreement, the application does not provide adequate certainty that the development qualifies for exemption from BNG obligations. As such, the proposal is contrary to the Environment Act 2021 and Merton Local Plan policy O15.3.",
    "Reason : 3 - In the absence of a legal agreement securing a carbon offset contribution, the application fails to demonstrate compliance with the Mayor�s net-zero carbon target contrary to Merton Local Plan policy CC2.2.",
    "Reason : 4 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\r\n\"\tThe application was considered to be fundamentally contrary to the provisions of the Development Plan and the NPPF, and there were not considered to be any solutions to resolve this conflict. \r\n"
  ],
